        "reasoning": "Original DSMZ 897, 1092 and 854 specify powdered sulfur at the respective 5, 3 and 10 g/L recipe levels and distinguish it from sulfide stock additions. Official CHEBI:33403 denotes elemental sulfur, not sulfur compounds or sulfide. Powder describes physical form; a specific S8 allotrope is not inferred. Existing Sulfur and its retired duplicates need survivor-aware handling, so the proposal names the active Sulfur owner and retains publication holds.",
        "applicability": "Individually reviewed source case 62: 'Sulfur (powdered)'; all 4 original occurrence IDs and full frozen recipe contexts are retained in RS-062-FROZEN. Primary references are scoped to those exact recipes or explicitly identified chemical/product candidates; no identity or concentration is transferred to a different preparation. This review preserves every inherited source/native hold and does not approve roles or release.",
