        },
        "occurrence_ids": [],
        "disposition": "unresolved",
        "reasoning": "All104 admitted media rows across103 media and29 overlapping solution rows specify Na2B4O7 x10H2O; the exact frozen source rows and full recipe bodies are preserved. One row in DSMZ770 is explicitly a0.1%w/v stock added at1.8ml, also confirmed by the original PDF, and cannot be treated as neat hydrate. The other source contexts retain the decahydrate reagent formula. The maintained owner and official CHEBI:131366 name decahydrate, yet its current formula10H2O.H4B4O9.2Na and structure expand to Na2B4H24O19, two H2O more than source Na2B4O7·10H2O (Na2B4H20O17). A label/CAS match therefore cannot approve the current exact assertion or imported chemical properties. Completeness reassessment: The source conventional sodium tetraborate decahydrate formula Na2B4O7·10H2O and structural borax formula Na2[B4O5(OH)4]·8H2O denote the same bulk material. Gainsford etal2008 DOI10.1107/S1600536808010441 explicitly identifies sodium tetraborate decahydrate as the latter structural formula, with Mr381.38. Official CHEBI38888 has that structural formula and381.371 mass; its octahydrate label counts the eight molecular waters after hydroxylation and does not mean Na2B4O7·8H2O. Official supplier CAS1303-96-4/Na2B4O7·10H2O/MW381.37 independently corroborates supplied form. CHEBI131366 and86222 instead contain two excess waters and remain upstream defects. This identity proposal covers explicitly weighed decahydrate reagent contexts; DSMZ7700.1%w/v stock remains a distinct preparation, so no global mediadive.ingredient:196 exact redirect is approved. MIM #1168 dependency closure: the three UW stocks explicitly name sodium tetraborate decahydrate at 0.0177 g/L in primary Mixes rows 1612, 1627 and 1643. Three guarded dependent proposals retain this exact component and quantity while replacing its catalog reference with the corrected CHEBI:38888 owner. Full-catalog regression reproduces three orphaned references from borax alone and zero after these dependent proposals; this does not approve unrelated inherited stock claims.",
        "applicability": "Applies only to this exact source profile and source_case_id, preserving its raw label and frozen count definition. All admitted recipe contexts and embedded downstream holds are bound by the case evidence. Listed owner records are inspected current candidates; a candidate is approved only to the narrow scope expressly stated in reasoning. Registry correspondence does not approve external chemistry, whole owner records, biological claims or complete SSSOM payloads.",
