    "decisions": [
      {
        "case_id": "CM_NAME:7e0f3c697acecd416fe5609a3a1bc3f829d96aebd6d89fad7a824a176cc39d8f",
        "case_input_sha256": "562d3b5da82d361baf453d8bdd2059a9d447636193cf9732c47349b39470fbe8",
        "source": {
          "source": "culturemech",
          "source_case_id": "As2O3",
          "source_label": "As2O3",
          "raw_source_label": "As2O3"
        },
        "occurrence_ids": [
          "CM_OCC:29255b71d40b900e7b36d10a85c9d0926bab32ccce15c85d22b7183e900cd0a3",
          "CM_OCC:9594ba2c3c61160476ae2da91f6f77ccf0f019a36dcfcd368043fd8845751064"
        ],
        "disposition": "new_distinct_ingredient_proposal",
        "reasoning": "Original CCAP UCM specifies As2O3 at two preparation levels: 0.000093 g/L in the trace-element stock and 0.093 g per 100 mL in alkaline primary stock 2, of which 0.1 mL/L enters the trace stock. These are not two independent final-medium doses. CHEBI:30621 is named diarsenic trioxide but represents molecular As4O6; the recipe uses empirical As2O3. An arsenite-ion identity cannot replace the supplied oxide. The explicit ChEBI definition covers the 2:3 arsenic/oxygen ratio, and PubChemCID14888 uses empiricalAs2O3 while retaining As4O6 among descriptors. The two-fold molecular depiction therefore does not by itself create a different source oxide identity. A minimal exactCHEBI:30621 owner is proposed without importing molecular mass, structure or a particular polymorph. The alkaline stock remains a separate preparation.",
        "applicability": "Individually reviewed source case 74: 'As2O3'; all 2 original occurrence IDs and full frozen recipe contexts are retained in RS-074-FROZEN. Primary references are scoped to those exact recipes or explicitly identified chemical/product candidates; no identity or concentration is transferred to a different preparation. This review preserves every inherited source/native hold and does not approve roles or release.",
